## Solution

**The group and its law.** Let $g = \begin{bmatrix}1 & x\\ 0 & y\end{bmatrix}$, $y \neq 0$. Writing elements as pairs $(x,y)$, the product is
$$
(x,y)(x',y') \;=\; \bigl(x' + x\,y',\; y\,y'\bigr),
$$
since $\begin{bmatrix}1 & x\\ 0 & y\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}1 & x'\\ 0 & y'\end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix}1 & x'+xy'\\ 0 & yy'\end{bmatrix}$.

**Left Haar measure.** Left multiplication by $(a,b)$ is
$$
L_{(a,b)}(x,y) = (x + a\,y,\; b\,y).
$$
Its Jacobian is
$$
J_L = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & a \\ 0 & b \end{pmatrix}, \qquad |\det J_L| = |b|.
$$
A left-invariant density $\rho(x,y)$ must satisfy $\rho(x+ay,\,by)\,|b| = \rho(x,y)$. This forces $\rho$ to be independent of $x$ and to obey $\rho(by)\,|b| = \rho(y)$, giving $\rho(y) = c/|y|$. Thus the left Haar measure on $B$ is
$$
d\mu(x,y) = \frac{dx\,dy}{|y|}.
$$

**Right translation.** Right multiplication by $g = (a,b)$ is
$$
R_{(a,b)}(x,y) = (x,y)(a,b) = (a + x\,b,\; y\,b).
$$
Its Jacobian is
$$
J_R = \begin{pmatrix} b & 0 \\ 0 & b \end{pmatrix}, \qquad |\det J_R| = b^{2}.
$$

**Computing $\Delta(g)$.** By definition $\mu(Ag) = \Delta(g)\,\mu(A)$. Using the change of variables $q = R_g(p)$,
$$
\mu(Ag) = \int_{Ag}\frac{dq_x\,dq_y}{|q_y|}
        = \int_{A}\frac{1}{\bigl|\,y\,b\,\bigr|}\,b^{2}\,dp
        = \int_{A}\frac{b^{2}}{|y|\,|b|}\,dp
        = |b|\int_{A}\frac{dp}{|y|}
        = |b|\,\mu(A).
$$
Therefore
$$
\boxed{\;\Delta(g) = |b| = |y|\;}, \qquad g = \begin{bmatrix}1 & x\\ 0 & y\end{bmatrix}.
$$

**Consistency checks.**

*Homomorphism property.* The $y$-component of $(x,y)(x',y')$ is $yy'$, so $\Delta(gg') = |yy'| = |y|\,|y'| = \Delta(g)\Delta(g')$. ✓

*Inverse property.* $g^{-1} = \begin{bmatrix}1 & -x/y\\ 0 & 1/y\end{bmatrix}$ has $y$-component $1/y$, so $\Delta(g)\Delta(g^{-1}) = |y|\cdot|1/y| = 1$. ✓

*Consistency with the Borel modular function.* For a general upper-triangular matrix $\begin{bmatrix}a & *\\ 0 & c\end{bmatrix}$ the modular function is $|c/a|$. Here $a=1$, $c=y$, recovering $|y|$. ✓

